{
 "points": [
  {
   "id": "P1.1",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Central hypothesis is assumed via definition, making the theory nearly circular.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.2",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Theory does not explain which simplicity measure is right, why training implements it, or when it fails.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.3",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Title and abstract overreach relative to what is proved.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.4",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Diffusion experiment computes no complexity measure and compares no non-generalizing solutions.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.5",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "MLP non-generalizing models trained on contradictory targets, confounding the simplicity comparison.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.6",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Experiments do not test whether source-only training finds the min-norm generalizing solution.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.7",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Identity task is privileged and near-linear, so norm-minimality may not be generic.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.8",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Only one well-optimized MLP reported, without seed statistics.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.9",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Figure 2 could not be viewed.",
   "minor": true
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.10",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Assumptions A.1 and A.2 (bounded loss, bounded third derivative) fail for neural networks.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.11",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Assumption A.3 gap between minima effectively assumes a benign non-convex landscape.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.12",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Estimator is the global minimizer, so optimization is ignored.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.13",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Underparameterized fixed-d asymptotic regime is opposite to foundation models.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.14",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Convex smooth regularizer assumption unrelated to network structural complexity.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.15",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Conditions B.1/B.2 imply isolated strongly convex minima, unlike continuum of spurious solutions.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.16",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Condition C.3 requires tau at least 9; no example verifies C.1-C.3.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.17",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "No lower bound shows vanishing-gap exponent is sharp.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.18",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Symmetries violate C.3; proposed quotient-space fix only conjectured.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.19",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Sharp/minimax claims overstated; optimality inherited from prior work only for unique minimizer.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.20",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Sample-size thresholds polynomial in many constants; results may need very large n.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.21",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Regularization weight depends on unknown gap; adaptivity not discussed.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.22",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Rate stated in introduction inconsistent with theorem.",
   "minor": true
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.23",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Related work on implicit regularization and simplicity is thin; idea not new.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.24",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Experiments are small and lack details such as how target error is measured.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.25",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Duplicate entries in reference list.",
   "minor": true
  },
  {
   "id": "Q1.1",
   "reviewer": "Q1",
   "text": "Studied NLL loss is only a bound on the diffusion denoising score matching objective.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q1.2",
   "reviewer": "Q1",
   "text": "Simplicity principle should be evaluated directly on real diffusion models, not a simplified setting.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q1.3",
   "reviewer": "Q1",
   "text": "Assumptions like B.1 strong convexity are restrictive for deep networks.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q1.4",
   "reviewer": "Q1",
   "text": "Large gap between simplified theoretical framework and practical diffusion/foundation model settings.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q2.1",
   "reviewer": "Q2",
   "text": "Paper is difficult to follow.",
   "minor": true
  },
  {
   "id": "Q2.2",
   "reviewer": "Q2",
   "text": "Experiments not connected to theory; theorems not related back to experiments.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q2.3",
   "reviewer": "Q2",
   "text": "Theory not specific to diffusion; conditional generative models are effectively classifiers or regressors.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q2.4",
   "reviewer": "Q2",
   "text": "Diffusion experiment seems contrived, only to link the work to diffusion.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q2.5",
   "reviewer": "Q2",
   "text": "Section 4.1 notation is cluttered and should be cleaned up.",
   "minor": true
  },
  {
   "id": "Q2.6",
   "reviewer": "Q2",
   "text": "Simplicity metric R is not defined or elaborated.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q3.1",
   "reviewer": "Q3",
   "text": "Simplicity-generalization link validated only in ad hoc toy identity setting; may be artifact.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q3.2",
   "reviewer": "Q3",
   "text": "Theory does not formally derive or explain the simplicity-generalization association.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q3.3",
   "reviewer": "Q3",
   "text": "Theory tautological: assumes known simplicity metric, offers no guidance on identifying it.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q4.1",
   "reviewer": "Q4",
   "text": "Few experiments; simple MLP far from real large-scale tasks.",
   "minor": false
  }
 ],
